-- R30 - THEMATIC HOLD AND BOOK BRAKE: thematic cards are 1-to-3-month expressions, not closed on a view change in
-- their first 10 sessions unless a stop, target, signpost or linked question fires; a book-level drawdown brake
-- halves then stops new cards (both Macro Takeaways digests). Tactical cards unchanged.
-- Source: thread "Sharpen trading approach for January restart", 21 Nov 2026; the owner's "be free in terms of
-- whatever trades you want to put on ... and whatever tenure you want to select" (he follows the books from Jan 2027).
-- Proposed 21 Nov 2026 with dash.propose_rule; apply_after = Sun 22 Nov 2026 20:00 SGT unless "oppose R30".
-- The call below is the exact call that was run.
-- To put it in force before the Sunday window (one line in the Supabase SQL editor, project diiwqbxyhtgvozhncoef):
--   update dash.rules set status = 'in_force', decided_at = now(), apply_after = now() where rid = 'R30' and status = 'proposed';
select dash.propose_rule($j${"scope": "both", "title": "Thematic cards are 1-to-3-month expressions held past 10 sessions unless a stop, target or signpost fires; a book-level drawdown brake halves then stops new cards", "body": "THEMATIC HOLD AND BOOK BRAKE (owner's go-ahead of 21 Nov 2026, thread \"Sharpen trading approach for January restart\": he will follow the books with real money from January 2027 and left trade choice and tenor to the runs; December is the paper trial). Three parts. Tactical cards are unchanged.\n\n1. THEMATIC TENOR. A new THEMATIC card is expressed for a planned hold of 15 to 60 sessions. Its carded structure has a tenor of at least one month that covers the planned hold: an option or spread with premium = 1R (R01), or a forward or future rolled under R07; for a cash FX thematic card this replaces R07's usual 2-week tenor with an outright forward covering the planned hold, R07's carry and roll mechanics unchanged. A 1-week or 2-week structure is not a thematic expression; a view whose catalyst lands inside five sessions is carded as TACTICAL or not at all. A linear thematic stop sits beyond the wider of 2 ATR(20) daily and the named structural level; r/r and EV are computed on that stop. The card prints \"HOLD <planned sessions> · tenor <expiry or roll date>\" after the TREND line.\n\n2. NO EARLY VIEW CLOSE. In its first 10 sessions after fill a thematic card closes only on (a) its stop (v15), (b) its target, (c) one of its SIGNPOSTS met by a dated fact in the day's inputs (name the datum, source and value), or (d) the linked Qnn resolving against it. A contrary voice, one day's adverse move or a lower mark is printed as evidence, never as a close. R08's review-first step still runs; its outcome inside the 10 sessions is HOLD unless (a) to (d) apply.\n\n3. BOOK BRAKE, printed in the BOOK CHECK from the SCORECARD's cum R and peak (per-unit R). Drawdown from peak of 5R or more: every new card is size 0.5 (META size), whatever its tier. 8R or more: no new cards except HEDGE cards for 5 sessions, then size 0.5 until the book recovers half the drawdown. Print \"BRAKE: off\" or \"BRAKE: half size (DD <x>R)\" or \"BRAKE: no new cards until <date> (DD <x>R)\". The brake never closes an open card.\n\nScoring: the weekly review cuts thematic cards opened from 23 Nov 2026 by hold bucket (0-5, 6-10, 11+ sessions) and exit type beside the earlier cards. Interim read for the owner on 8 Jan 2027, before his first real trades; decision at 20 closed thematic cards under this rule or 28 Feb 2027.", "rationale": "On 21 Nov 2026 the owner said he will follow the Takeaways trades rigorously from January 2027 and left the choice of trades and tenor to the runs. The Fable book's own record says its losses sit in thematic cards that lived five sessions or less (stopped on tight stops or closed on a changed view) while thematic cards held 11 sessions or more made most of its R, and tactical washout cards were net positive. The AI-unwind theme was on the book for weeks but carded as 1-to-2-week structures that monetised little. So the thematic expression is lengthened and protected from early view closes, tactical cards stay as they are, and a book brake is added because real money will follow the book.", "evidence": "dash.trades model fable, 37 closed cards to 21 Nov 2026, cut by tclass x hold (filled to closed) x exit status; dash.book_state fable SCORECARD (cum R, peak, max DD, view-changed closes). Figures are kept out of the public repo.", "revert_if": "Revert if 5 thematic cards opened under this rule stop out in a row, if thematic cards opened under it lose more R in their first 10 sessions than the earlier thematic cards did over the same window by the 8 Jan read, or if a card is closed on a view change inside 10 sessions without (a) to (d) on 2 or more days.", "review_due": "2027-02-28", "source": "thread"}$j$::jsonb);
